    "id": "unified-example-downtime-factions",
    "name": "Downtime with competing faction proposals",
    "description": "Advance an authored bounded downtime period, collect faction proposals, check resource conflicts, guide arrival and commit the accepted time and public faction developments.\n\nSetup: Create public story-clock from the clock template and public JSON faction-developments as []. The authored duration is 480 story minutes; edit it to the actual agreed downtime. Two public faction proposals share one resource pool; schema validation bounds each use and local arithmetic rejects conflicting totals. Factions are proposals until Apply. Hidden offscreen simulation requires a separate permitted private store and explicit discovery leg. A retry of the same candidate neither advances time nor writes developments again.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
